{#-
  The per-node parameter declarations, and (phase-509 P2) the node's rank.

  Issue 1971 (RFC-0107 step 1) -- the node's launch REMAPS are no longer
  declared here: they are one flash table for the whole image
  (`launch_remap_table.jinja`), installed before the runner sets up any tier
  (`launch_remap_install.jinja`). One `nros_cpp_declare_remap` per rule per
  tier filled a 16-rule RAM table in every executor.

  ONE partial, included by both entry packs, because the statements are
  byte-identical C in both — only the executor expression differs, and the
  caller passes it in as `dexec` (phase-494: it is template text, so the
  template that writes it chooses it; it used to ride on a Rust view).

  What the caller puts in scope: `n`, the `LoweredNode`, and `dexec`, its
  executor expression. A C++ entry compiles these exact lines. Two copies would
  be two authored spellings of one call sequence, which is the defect
  phase-432 exists to remove; before this they were `emit_declare_remaps` and
  `emit_declare_params`, `pub(super)` string writers in `emit_c.rs` that
  `emit_cpp` called.

  ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING and belongs to the caller, not here. Both of these run
  BEFORE the component is constructed or configured: an rclcpp-shape
  constructor registers entities immediately (issue 0255) and reads
  `declare_parameter` initials immediately (issue 0745). Seeding params is
  independent of whether the param-SERVICES surface is enabled — the old
  emission sat inside the `param_services` gate and AFTER construction, so a
  plan without param services silently dropped every launch param.

  issue 1272 -- a parameter seed lands on ITS node. Both packs emit these
  calls BEFORE the node is created, so the seed is for the NEXT node the
  executor builds. phase-509 P9b: the seed NAMES that node
  (`nros_cpp_declare_node_param`) and the shim resolves its index from the
  executor itself; a build-time index restarted per tier, and under RFC-0108's
  one executor per core every level's setup registers on the same executor,
  so the second level's seeds named a node that was not next and its setup
  failed. A seed for another node on the index the previous node was seeded
  for (that node was never built) is refused, as 1272 refused a stale index.

  Indentation is eight spaces because both callers open a node block at four.
  It is written here rather than passed in: a caller that needed a different
  depth would be emitting these somewhere they do not belong.
-#}
{#- phase-509 P2 (RFC-0108 D2) -- the node's contract rank, seeded before the
    node is created so every callback it registers dispatches in rank order
    inside its bucket. Only when the entry derived ranks: a node with none
    holds rank 0, today's order. #}
{%- if n.rank is not none %}
        {
            nros_cpp_ret_t rrc = nros_cpp_bind_node_rank({{ dexec }}, "{{ n.name | c_str }}", "{{ n.namespace | c_str }}", {{ n.rank }}u);
            if (rrc != NROS_CPP_RET_OK) return (int32_t)rrc;
        }
{%- endif %}
{%- for p in n.params %}
        {
            nros_cpp_ret_t prc = nros_cpp_declare_node_param({{ dexec }}, "{{ n.name | c_str }}", "{{ p[0] | c_str }}", "{{ p[1] | c_str }}");
            if (prc != NROS_CPP_RET_OK) return (int32_t)prc;
        }
{%- endfor -%}
